{{sectionNumber}} Session-Controlled BYOD Architecture

The {{tenant_variant}} tenant operates a session-controlled Bring Your Own Device (BYOD) architecture. Under this model, personally owned devices access CUI exclusively through browser-based sessions governed by Conditional Access application-enforced restrictions. No CUI is stored, cached, or processed on the endpoint device itself; all data interaction occurs within the cloud session boundary{{azure_mention}}.

Four enforcement mechanisms underpin this architecture:

1. Conditional Access App Control: {{ca_app_control_policies_summary}}
2. Non-Browser Client Block: {{non_browser_block_policy_summary}}
3. Data Loss Prevention: {{dlp_policies_summary}}
4. Sensitivity Labels: {{sensitivity_labels_summary}}

Enforcement was verified active as of {{verification_date}}.

Organizations that do not issue managed endpoints to all CUI-handling personnel may opt out of device-management controls (e.g., MDM enrollment, Intune compliance) when the session-controlled BYOD architecture provides equivalent or superior data protection through the four mechanisms listed above.
